WinForms Designer parser errors/warnings log
Generated during analysis of the supplied Form1 designer code.

Errors that prevented parsing:
1. Instantiations used bare field names without "this." (e.g. "menuStrip1 = new MenuStrip();"). Parser's NewControlRegex required "this.".
2. Property assignments used bare field names (e.g. "menuStrip1.Location = ..."). PropertyAssignRegex required "this.".
3. Root-level assignments omitted "this." (e.g. "AutoScaleMode = ...", "Controls.Add(menuStrip1)", "MainMenuStrip = menuStrip1"). RootPropertyAssignRegex required "this.".
4. Event handlers used bare fields (e.g. "openDaysToolStripMenuItem.Click += ..."). EventAssignRegex required "this.".
5. Controls were added without "this." ("Controls.Add(menuStrip1)"). ControlsAddRegex required "this.".
6. ToolStrip items were added via Items.AddRange/DropDownItems.AddRange; parser only handled Controls.Add/Controls.AddRange.
7. ToolStripMenuItem nested items were not created in the live tree (CreateStripItem did not recurse).
8. Generator emitted ".Items.AddRange" for ToolStripMenuItem parents (should be DropDownItems) and suspended layout on ToolStripItems.
9. Short type names ("new Size", "new Point") were not recognized by TryParseSize/TryParsePoint.
10. AutoScaleMode was emitted twice in generated code.

Fixes applied:
- Made "this." optional in all relevant regexes with negative lookbehinds.
- Added Items/DropDownItems Add/AddRange parsing and hierarchy building.
- Updated CreateStripItem to handle parent ToolStrip/ToolStripMenuItem and recurse.
- Updated generator to use DropDownItems for ToolStripDropDownItem parents.
- Excluded non-Control nodes from layout suspend/resume.
- Supported short "Size"/"Point"/"SizeF" names.
- Prevented duplicate AutoScaleMode emission.
- Improved reference property handling for bare field names.

Result: Sample parses into Form1 -> menuStrip1 -> toolsToolStripMenuItem -> openDaysToolStripMenuItem; generated project builds successfully.